Q: how can i do a alias in powershell to start notepad++ A: <p>I have been playing around with adding a function to my profile (Powershell 7)</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>notepad $PROFILE
</code></pre>
<p>add:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code># notepad++
function np {
 if ($args.Count -lt 1) { start notepad++ }

 $resolvedArgs = @()
 foreach ($arg in $args) {
    Try {        
        $path = $ExecutionContext.SessionState.Path.GetUnresolvedProviderPathFromPSPath($arg)
        $normalizedPath = ($path.ToString()).Trim()
        $resolvedArgs += $normalizedPath
    }
    Catch {
        Write-Warning &quot;$($arg) cannot be resolved&quot;
    }
 }  

 start notepad++ $resolvedArgs
}
</code></pre>
<p>example usage:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>#no args
np

#multiple args with some resolution
np ~/.ssh/config $Profile a_brand_new_file.txt AnExistingFile.txt 
</code></pre>
